From a2fdbde4956f75a3ade83cb5e7a394f9791ad8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 053/240] Bugfix: synchronize threads on allocation failure and
 overflow, and report errors in `bgraphBipartDf()` [report R. Perry]

When a thread could not allocate its local arrays, it jumped over the
reduction of external gain sums, so that threads went out of step with
respect to barriers: `bgraphBipartDf()` returned with thread data that
were never computed, and some worker thread could re-run the loop on
the freed data. When the diffusion process overflowed, the vertex index
was set to the end of the vertex run before the last value was stored,
which read past the thread-local array and wrote into the first vertex
of the next thread (or past the diffusion arrays), and the loop index
then skipped the reduction of anchor contributions, with the same loss
of synchronization. Moreover, the shared abort flag could be set by a
fast thread while slower threads were still testing it for the previous
pass or for the allocation phase, which made them leave early.
Synchronize threads right after the local allocation, as in
`bgraphBipartGa()`, and return an error when some thread could not do
its work. On overflow, store the last value of the run in place, and
record the pass number in the thread data block, so that all threads
halt at the end of the same pass and keep the last valid state.

Refs: SEP-14
---
 src/libscotch/bgraph_bipart_df.c | 78 ++++++++++++++++++++------------
 src/libscotch/bgraph_bipart_df.h |  7 +--
 2 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

